// semantic_errors.med
// MedRoute Example 4 — Intentional Semantic Errors Demo
// ============================================================
// This program has VALID SYNTAX but INVALID SEMANTICS.
// The compiler must detect and report all semantic violations.
//
// Expected: SEMANTIC_ERROR status

// Register patient P101
PATIENT P101
LOCATION P101 "Sector 21"

// ERROR 1: Duplicate patient registration
PATIENT P101

// ERROR 2: Dispatch with unregistered ambulance A99
DISPATCH A99 P101

// Register ambulance correctly
AMBULANCE A12
HOSPITAL H01 "General Hospital"

// Dispatch OK
DISPATCH A12 P101

// ERROR 3: Dispatch again — ambulance A12 already DISPATCHED
DISPATCH A12 P101

// ERROR 4: ARRIVE before dispatch on a different (nonexistent) ambulance
ARRIVE A50

// ERROR 5: TRANSFER before ambulance has arrived (A12 is still DISPATCHED, not ARRIVED)
TRANSFER P101 H01

// ERROR 6: Invalid severity value
PATIENT P102
SEVERITY P102 EXTREME

// ERROR 7: ROUTE to unregistered hospital
ROUTE A12 H99

REPORT
